SUMMARY:Planning in Microsoft Fabric: From Semantic Models to Integrated P
 lanning
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nPlanning has long lived outside the
  analytics stack—disconnected from the data\, metrics\, and governance t
 eams rely on every day. In this session\, we’ll introduce Planning in Mi
 crosoft Fabric\, a new native capability that brings budgeting\, forecasti
 ng\, and scenario modeling directly into the Fabric platform.\n\nYou’ll 
 learn how Planning in Fabric connects seamlessly to Power BI semantic mode
 ls\, OneLake\, and Fabric SQL\, enabling business and finance teams to pla
 n on governed\, real‑time data—without exports\, duplication\, or frag
 ile integrations. We’ll walk through the core concepts\, typical use cas
 es\, and how Planning fits into the broader Fabric vision of unifying hist
 orical insights with future‑looking decisions.\n\nWhether you’re a dat
 a professional\, analyst\, or business leader\, this session will help you
  understand how Planning in Fabric can turn insights into action—faster 
 and with confidence\n\n📌 This session is a part of a series! Learn more
  [here](https://developer.microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-1448/?wt.mc_id=me
 etup_S-1448_webpage_reactor)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3140
 46561/
