SUMMARY:Azure Decoded: Ship & Monetize Agents—Architecture\, Readiness\,
  Release
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nYour agent works. Now make it shipp
 able.\n\nTurning an agent MVP into a Marketplace-ready solution is not jus
 t a packaging exercise—it’s a production\, security\, and scale proble
 m. In this must‑see session\, we’ll break down what it really takes to
  go from prototype to publishable product\, mapping architecture and opera
 tional decisions directly to commercialization outcomes.\n\nYou’ll get a
  no‑nonsense walkthrough of the critical readiness checkpoints\, real-wo
 rld requirements for scalability\, security\, reliability\, and governance
 \, and the end‑to‑end Marketplace publishing and release process—so 
 there are no surprises when you’re ready to ship.\n\nWalk away with a ba
 ttle‑tested technical checklist\, concrete next steps\, and the exact re
 sources needed to confidently move from MVP to Marketplace. Built for deve
 lopers. Critical for IT pros. Required watching if you plan to publish.\n\
 n**What you'll learn:**\n\n* How to align technical readiness with busines
 s goals\n* A simplified view of the publishing workflow (Microsoft Foundry
  → Marketplace publishing\n* Next-step assets to reduce first-publish fr
 iction (readiness checklists + GTM/publishing guides)\n\nWho should attend
 : Developers and Founders who want to ship agents as a commercial product 
 (plus technical decision makers supporting that journey)
